---
source: tests/cli_input.rs
expression: "report.join(\"\\n\\n\")"
---
$ pouncer 
pouncer: no patterns: pass at least one --regex or --preset (nothing matches by default)

$ pouncer --preset nope
pouncer: unknown --preset "nope"; available: url, email, ipv4, ipv6, path, sha, uuid, filepos, hostport, hex, mdlink, jwt, pod, number

$ pouncer --regex (
pouncer: invalid regex "(": regex parse error:
    (
    ^
error: unclosed group

$ pouncer --regex a --capture 1
pouncer: --capture 1: --regex "a" has no group 1

$ pouncer --preset url --alphabet aa
pouncer: invalid --alphabet: alphabet repeats the character 'a'

$ pouncer --preset url --multi --upper-action open
pouncer: --upper-action needs a single pick; it has no meaning with --multi

$ pouncer --preset url --upper-action open --alphabet abC
pouncer: --upper-action reads an uppercase key as the alternate action, so --alphabet must be lowercase

$ pouncer --preset url --hint-bg nope
error: invalid value 'nope' for '--hint-bg <COLOR>': unknown color "nope"; expected a name (e.g. red, dark_blue), 0-255, or #rrggbb

For more information, try '--help'.

$ pouncer --preset url --cols 0
error: invalid value '0' for '--cols <N>': 0 is not in 1..=65535

For more information, try '--help'.
